## qf-phil2 | Quick-fire: ideas 2 | philo | 0 | - | qf-phil
quiz 3 | "The unexamined life is not worth living" is attributed to…
* Socrates
o Plato
o Aristotle
o Seneca
= Said at his trial, as recorded by Plato in the Apology.
> Next

quiz 3 | Occam's razor favours…
* The explanation with the fewest assumptions
o The most detailed explanation
o The oldest explanation
o Expert opinion
= A rule of thumb, not a proof.
> Next

quiz 3 | Empiricism holds that knowledge comes mainly from…
* Experience
o Reason alone
o Revelation
o Intuition
= Locke, Berkeley and Hume were classic empiricists.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which philosopher said "Hell is other people"?
* Jean-Paul Sartre
o Albert Camus
o Friedrich Nietzsche
o Søren Kierkegaard
= From the play No Exit (1944).
> Next

quiz 4 | A "tabula rasa" is…
* A blank slate: the mind at birth, in Locke's view
o A logical contradiction
o A moral rule
o A Greek tablet
= Contrasted with innate ideas.
> Next

quiz 4 | Stoicism was founded in Athens by…
* Zeno of Citium
o Epicurus
o Diogenes
o Pythagoras
= Named after the Stoa Poikile, a painted porch where he taught.
> Next

quiz 4 | Epicurus taught that the goal of life is…
* Pleasure, understood as freedom from pain and anxiety
o Wealth
o Duty
o Glory
= Simple pleasures, friendship and calm, not indulgence.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which thought experiment involves a demon deceiving you about everything?
* Descartes' evil demon
o Laplace's demon
o Maxwell's demon
o Socrates' daemon
= A sceptical scenario that led to "I think, therefore I am".
> More quick-fire next

## qf-econ2 | Quick-fire: money 2 | econ | 0 | - | qf-econ
quiz 3 | Compound interest means…
* Earning interest on previous interest
o Interest that never changes
o Interest paid only at the end
o Interest charged on loans only
= Einstein is often (probably wrongly) credited with calling it the eighth wonder of the world.
> Next

quiz 3 | What does "diversification" reduce?
* Risk from any single investment
o All risk entirely
o Returns to zero
o Taxes
= Don't put all your eggs in one basket.
> Next

quiz 3 | A stock market "bear market" is…
* A fall of 20% or more from a recent high
o A rising market
o A market closed for holidays
o A market for commodities
= A bull market is a sustained rise.
> Next

quiz 4 | At 6% annual return, roughly how long to double money (Rule of 72)?
* 12 years
o 6 years
o 72 years
o 20 years
= 72 ÷ 6.
> Next

quiz 4 | What is an "externality"?
* A cost or benefit affecting people outside a transaction
o An import tax
o A foreign investment
o A company's overseas office
= Pollution is the classic negative externality.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which currency is used by the most countries (officially)?
* The euro
o The US dollar
o The pound
o The yen
= About 20 EU countries plus several others. Many more use the dollar unofficially or alongside their own.
> Next

quiz 4 | What does "Goodhart's law" warn about?
* Measures becoming bad once they're targets
o Inflation becoming permanent
o Markets always crashing
o Monopolies forming
= Teaching to the test is a classic example.
> Next

quiz 4 | What does a higher inflation rate do to the value of cash savings?
* Erodes their real value
o Increases their value
o Has no effect
o Doubles them
= Unless interest rates keep up.
> More quick-fire next

## qf-space2 | Quick-fire: space 2 | physics | 0 | - | qf-sci2
quiz 3 | What's at the centre of the Milky Way?
* A supermassive black hole
o The Sun
o A neutron star
o An empty void
= Sagittarius A*, about 4 million solar masses.
> Next

quiz 3 | What are Saturn's rings mainly made of?
* Ice
o Gas
o Iron
o Dust only
= Chunks from grains to houses in size.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which planet spins on its side?
* Uranus
o Neptune
o Saturn
o Venus
= Axial tilt about 98°, probably from a huge ancient collision.
> Next

quiz 4 | What is a supernova?
* The explosive death of a star
o The birth of a star
o A comet hitting a planet
o A bright planet
= Briefly it can outshine an entire galaxy.
> Next

quiz 4 | What causes a solar eclipse?
* The Moon passing between Earth and the Sun
o Earth passing between the Sun and the Moon
o Clouds on the Sun
o Venus crossing the Sun
= Earth between them gives a lunar eclipse.
> Next

quiz 4 | Why can total solar eclipses happen at all?
* The Sun is about 400× wider than the Moon but also about 400× farther away
o The Moon is bigger than the Sun
o The Sun shrinks during eclipses
o Earth's shadow is large
= A coincidence: they appear almost the same size in our sky.
> Next

quiz 4 | What's the Kármán line?
* A common boundary of space, 100 km up
o The edge of the solar system
o The orbit of the Moon
o The equator of the Sun
= A convention; the US often uses 80 km.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which spacecraft is farthest from Earth?
* Voyager 1
o Voyager 2
o New Horizons
o Pioneer 10
= Over 24 billion km away and counting.
> More quick-fire next

