quiz 3 | What are the three primary colours of light (additive)?
* Red, green, blue
o Red, yellow, blue
o Cyan, magenta, yellow
o Black, white, grey
= Screens mix RGB. Painters' traditional primaries are red, yellow and blue.
> Next

quiz 4 | Who wrote the opera The Magic Flute?
* Mozart
o Verdi
o Wagner
o Puccini
= 1791, the year he died.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which artist cut off part of his own ear?
* Vincent van Gogh
o Paul Gauguin
o Edvard Munch
o Pablo Picasso
= December 1888, in Arles, after a quarrel with Gauguin.
> Next

quiz 4 | A haiku traditionally has how many lines?
* 3
o 5
o 14
o 4
= In English often 5-7-5 syllables.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which musical instrument has 47 strings and 7 pedals (concert version)?
* Harp
o Piano
o Guitar
o Cello
= The pedals change each string's pitch by semitones.
> Next

quiz 4 | Who painted Guernica?
* Pablo Picasso
o Joan Miró
o Salvador Dalí
o Diego Rivera
= 1937, responding to the bombing of the Basque town.
> Quick-fire round nine complete
